# Runtime Image Build — `rfipconfig-be` (Shipwright PoC)

Builds the **.NET runtime image** for `rfipconfig-be` using Builds for Red Hat
OpenShift (Shipwright), following the same pattern proven on the builder image
build. This is the second of two image builds required before the build
pipeline task (Jenkins/Argo + BuildRun + Argo CD) begins.

**Migration requirements implemented here:**

1. Base image pulled from `quay.hobbylobby.corp` (not the legacy `hl-images` namespace)
2. Entrypoint script extracted from the legacy base64-encoded variable into a
   real, version-controlled file (`entrypoint.sh`)
3. Registry credentials handled via a Kubernetes Secret (`pipeline-push-secret`),
   never via environment variables

---

## Why a different strategy than the builder image

The builder image build used the custom **s2i** ClusterBuildStrategy because it
needed the `s2i-generate` step (source → Dockerfile generation). The runtime
image has **no source to compile** — it is a base image plus an entrypoint
script — so it uses a plain Dockerfile build via a custom **`buildah-hl`**
ClusterBuildStrategy.

The operator ships a built-in cluster-level `buildah` strategy, but it does not
mount our internal CA, so pulls from `quay.hobbylobby.corp` would fail with
x509 errors. `buildah-hl` is a copy of the `buildah` step from `s2i.yaml`,
keeping the `hobbylobby.corp` CA configMap mount that `SSL_CERT_FILE` points at.

---

## Files

| File | Kind | Purpose |
|------|------|---------|
| `buildah-hl.yaml` | ClusterBuildStrategy | Dockerfile build via buildah, with the internal CA configMap mounted at `/etc/pki/ca-trust/extracted/trust-manager` |
| `rfipconfig-be-runtime.yaml` | Build | Runtime image build definition. Reuses `SSL_CERT_FILE`, `pipeline-push-secret`, push to `openshift-builds` |
| `buildrun-runtime.yaml` | BuildRun | One-shot run trigger (`generateName`, `pipeline` SA) |
| `Dockerfile` | — | Runtime image content (base image + entrypoint) |
| `entrypoint.sh` | — | **To be added** — decoded from the legacy base64 variable |

