## Prerequisites

- Builds for Red Hat OpenShift Operator installed (`openshift-builds-operator.v1.8.1`)
- `pipeline` ServiceAccount in `openshift-builds` with the
  `rb-pipeline-image-builder` RoleBinding (`system:image-builder`) — already in `rbac.yaml`
- `pipeline-push-secret` (`kubernetes.io/dockerconfigjson`) in `openshift-builds`
- `hobbylobby.corp` CA configMap in `openshift-builds`
- Cluster-admin access for Step 2 (ClusterBuildStrategy is cluster-scoped;
  only cluster admins have write access to it)
- Valid `oc` session (`oc whoami` — tokens expire ~24h)

---

## Steps

### Step 1 — Commit the runtime image content to Git

```bash
mkdir runtime-image/
# Add Dockerfile; set FROM to the exact runtime base image on quay.hobbylobby.corp

# Extract the entrypoint script from the legacy base64 variable:
echo "<BASE64_VALUE>" | base64 -d > runtime-image/entrypoint.sh
```

Review `entrypoint.sh` for embedded secrets **before** committing, then commit
and push.

### Step 2 — Apply the custom ClusterBuildStrategy

Fill in first:
- `steps[0].image` → copy the buildah image from the `buildah` step in `s2i.yaml`
- Confirm the CA configMap name matches what `s2i.yaml` mounts

```bash
oc apply -f buildah-hl.yaml
oc get clusterbuildstrategy buildah-hl
```

### Step 3 — Apply the Build

Fill in first:
- `source.git.url` + `cloneSecret` (reuse from `rfipconfig-be.yaml` if same repo)
- `contextDir: runtime-image/`

```bash
oc apply -f rfipconfig-be-runtime.yaml
oc get builds.shipwright.io rfipconfig-be-runtime-image -n openshift-builds
```

> Always use the fully qualified `builds.shipwright.io` — bare `oc get build`
> resolves to the legacy `build.openshift.io` type.

### Step 4 — Run the BuildRun

```bash
oc create -f buildrun-runtime.yaml    # create, NOT apply (generateName)
oc get buildruns.shipwright.io -n openshift-builds -w
```

### Step 5 — Verify

```bash
oc get pods -n openshift-builds
oc logs -f <buildrun-pod-name> -n openshift-builds --all-containers
oc get istag -n openshift-builds | grep rfipconfig-be-runtime
```

**Success checklist:**

- [ ] `step-buildah` log: `Trying to pull quay.hobbylobby.corp/...` proceeds with **no x509 error**
- [ ] `[INFO] Pushing image ...` completes without `authentication required`
- [ ] `oc get buildruns.shipwright.io` shows `SUCCEEDED=True`
- [ ] `oc get istag -n openshift-builds` shows the `rfipconfig-be-runtime` tag
- [ ] Status checked via **CLI, not the console BuildRun detail page**
      (OCPBUGS-84214 UI crash still open on operator v1.8.1)

